 passes through the point $\\mathbf{x}_0$ at $t=t_0.$\n\nTo solve an IVP, we proceed as follows:\n\n- Find the general solution of the system $\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t){:}$ \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t)=c_1\\mathbf{x}_1(t)+c_2\\mathbf{x}_2(t)\n$$\n\n- Substitute $t=t_0$ into the general solution and use the initial condition $\\mathbf{x}(t_0)=\\mathbf{x}_0{:}$\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t_0)=c_1\\mathbf{x}_1(t_0)+c_2\\mathbf{x}_2(t_0)\n\\qquad\\Rightarrow\\qquad\nc_1\\mathbf{x}_1(t_0)+c_2\\mathbf{x}_2(t_0)=\\mathbf{x}_0\n$$\n\n- Solve the resulting linear system for $c_1$ and $c_2,$ then substitute those values back into $\\mathbf{x}(t).$\n\nThe definition (and the procedure) above generalizes directly to the $n\\times n$ case.\n\nLet's see some concrete examples of solving an IVP." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130360 #edb/ref 1065 3651 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130360 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "92ec67c9-079c-5825-825b-08cca4b2cf25" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130360 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133765 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048169 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133765 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048701 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133765 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048861 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133765 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186134424 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133765 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186134425 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133765 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186272190 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133765 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186329732 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133765 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186329733 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133765 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186329734 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133765 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186329735 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133765 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186329739 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133765 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186338874 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133